      "id": 1,
      "text": "Creswell was named for John Creswell, who served as the twenty-third United States Postmaster General.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creswell%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before European settlers arrived, the land that is now Creswell was home to the Kalapuya Native American tribe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitoregon.com/cities/creswell-oregon/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Creswell was established in 1872 when the Oregon and California Railroad was built through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitoregon.com/cities/creswell-oregon/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first store and a post office both opened in Creswell in 1872, helping the town grow quickly.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creswell%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Creswell is located in the Willamette Valley of Lane County, about twelve miles south of Eugene.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
